    {
      "name": "monaco-editor-type-fox",
      "type": "registry:component",
      "title": "Monaco Editor Type Fox",
      "description": "Editable MoyaForge monaco-editor-type-fox source. Components import their own CSS.",
      "docs": "# MonacoEditorTypeFox\n\nMulti-file editor using `@typefox/monaco-editor-react` and VS Code services.\n\nThe CLI and shadcn install runtime dependencies. In an existing React app:\n\n```sh\nnpm install @typefox/monaco-editor-react@~8.0.2 monaco-languageclient@~11.0.2 @codingame/monaco-vscode-editor-api@^37.6.1 lucide-react\n```\n\nConfigure Monaco workers before mounting the editor. The documentation's `setup.ts` shows a Vite setup with optional standalone TypeScript, CSS, HTML, and JSON language features; install every feature package imported by that setup at version `^37.6.1`.\n\nImport `MonacoEditorTypeFox` from `./MonacoEditorTypeFox`. Pass `files` with unique names, optional per-file `readOnly`, and `onSave` to persist changes. `readOnly` locks the workspace. `vscodeApiConfig` customizes host services; all instances share the application's VS Code service initialization.\n",
      "dependencies": [
        "@codingame/monaco-vscode-editor-api@^37.6.1",
        "@typefox/monaco-editor-react@~8.0.2",
        "lucide-react@^1.56.0",
        "monaco-languageclient@~11.0.2",
        "react@>=18"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
